  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 902.13 Geomorphic compatibility",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 902.13 “Geomorphic compatibility” means the long-term ability of a stream crossing to:\n\n(a) Minimize potential for obstruction by sediment, wood, and debris;\n\n(b) Preserve the natural alignment of the stream; and\n\n(c) Accommodate the entrenchment ratio, bank full depth, and channel slope of the stream.\n\nSource. #12809, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt900.html"
